{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":9,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 9:1"},"Then Job answered and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 9:2"},"I know ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it is"]}," so of a truth: but how should man be just with God? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 9:3"},"If he will contend with him, he cannot answer him one of a thousand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 9:4"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["He is"]}," wise in heart, and mighty in strength: who hath hardened ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["himself"]}," against him, and hath prospered? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 9:5"},"Which removeth the mountains, and they know not: which overturneth them in his anger. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 9:6"},"Which shaketh the earth out of her place, and the pillars thereof tremble. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 9:7"},"Which commandeth the sun, and it riseth not; and sealeth up the stars. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 9:8"},"Which alone spreadeth out the heavens, and treadeth upon the waves of the sea. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 9:9"},"Which maketh Arcturus, Orion, and Pleiades, and the chambers of the south. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 9:10"},"Which doeth great things past finding out; yea, and wonders without number. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 9:11"},"Lo, he goeth by me, and I see ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["him"]}," not: he passeth on also, but I perceive him not. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 9:12"},"Behold, he taketh away, who can hinder him? who will say unto him, What doest thou? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 9:13"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["If"]}," God will not withdraw his anger, the proud helpers do stoop under him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 9:14"},"How much less shall I answer him, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," choose out my words ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to reason"]}," with him? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 9:15"},"Whom, though I were righteous, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yet"]}," would I not answer, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but"]}," I would make supplication to my judge. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 9:16"},"If I had called, and he had answered me; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yet"]}," would I not believe that he had hearkened unto my voice. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 9:17"},"For he breaketh me with a tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 9:18"},"He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 9:19"},"If ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["I speak"]}," of strength, lo, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["he is"]}," strong: and if of judgment, who shall set me a time ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to plead? "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 9:20"},"If I justify myself, mine own mouth shall condemn me: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["if I say, I am"]}," perfect, it shall also prove me perverse. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 9:21"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Though"]}," I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["were"]}," perfect, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yet"]}," would I not know my soul: I would despise my life. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 9:22"},"This ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," one ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thing,"]}," therefore I said ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it, "]},"He destroyeth the perfect and the wicked. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 9:23"},"If the scourge slay suddenly, he will laugh at the trial of the innocent. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 9:24"},"The earth is given into the hand of the wicked: he covereth the faces of the judges thereof; if not, where, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," who ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," he? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 9:25"},"Now my days are swifter than a post: they flee away, they see no good. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"JOB 9:26"},"They are passed away as the swift ships: as the eagle ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that "]},"hasteth to the prey. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"JOB 9:27"},"If I say, I will forget my complaint, I will leave off my heaviness, and comfort ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["myself: "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"JOB 9:28"},"I am afraid of all my sorrows, I know that thou wilt not hold me innocent. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:28"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"29","sid":"JOB 9:29"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["If"]}," I be wicked, why then labour I in vain? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:29"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"30","sid":"JOB 9:30"},"If I wash myself with snow water, and make my hands never so clean; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:30"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"31","sid":"JOB 9:31"},"Yet shalt thou plunge me in the ditch, and mine own clothes shall abhor me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:31"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"32","sid":"JOB 9:32"},"For ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["he is"]}," not a man, as I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am, that"]}," I should answer him, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," we should come together in judgment. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:32"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"33","sid":"JOB 9:33"},"Neither is there any daysman betwixt us, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," might lay his hand upon us both. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:33"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"34","sid":"JOB 9:34"},"Let him take his rod away from me, and let not his fear terrify me: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:34"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"35","sid":"JOB 9:35"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Then"]}," would I speak, and not fear him; but ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it is "]},"not so with me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 9:35"}]}]}
